# fixtures/gen/EXPECTED.sha256 -- the pins for every generator under fixtures/gen/.
#
# 13-quality.md:588: "fixtures/gen/EXPECTED.sha256 pins each generator's output so a generator
# change is a one-line visible diff rather than a silent corpus change."
#
# Standard sha256sum format: digest, two spaces, a path relative to the WORKSPACE ROOT. Check the
# whole file from the workspace root with
#
#     sha256sum -c fixtures/gen/EXPECTED.sha256
#
# after regenerating both outputs, or regenerate and re-pin one line with
#
#     uv run python fixtures/gen/gen_5000p_pdf.py --pages 8 --print-sha256
#     uv run python fixtures/gen/gen_5000p_pdf.py --print-sha256
#     uv run python fixtures/gen/gen_incremental.py --manifest --print-sha256
#
# Neither output is committed: fixtures/generated/ is .gitignored (13-quality.md:588), and the
# 5,000-page file is ~29 MB against Tier A's 64 MB total (11-repo-layout.md:383).
#
# WHICH LINE IS CHECKED BY WHICH TEST
#   gen_8p.pdf     packages/omniweave-core/tests/unit/test_fixture_gen.py
#                  ::test_the_small_pin_is_the_digest_of_a_freshly_generated_eight_page_run
#                  ~0.1 s. The cheap check, and the one a developer runs while editing.
#   gen_5000p.pdf  packages/omniweave-core/tests/unit/test_fixture_gen.py
#                  ::test_the_default_pin_is_the_digest_of_a_freshly_generated_five_thousand_page_run
#                  ~1.2 s and ~29 MB of temporary file. Run anyway: a pin nothing checks is the
#                  silent corpus change arriving by the front door.
#   roster-step0   packages/omniweave-core/tests/unit/test_fixture_incremental.py
#                  ::test_the_pin_is_the_digest_of_a_freshly_generated_initial_roster
#                  ~0.3 s. G19's 300-document corpus, pinned through a MANIFEST rather than
#                  document by document: 300 lines that all turn over together would make a
#                  corpus change unreadable, and this file's whole purpose is that a corpus
#                  change is "a one-line visible diff" (13-quality.md:588).
#   reference/*    bench/serve/test_corpora.py
#                  ::test_every_reference_corpus_is_its_pin_at_both_scales
#                  ~1.5 s for all six. ADR-14 D14.1's three corpora at both scales, each pinned
#                  through its MANIFEST (`sha256  relpath` per file), as the roster is.
#   office-200     packages/omniweave-office/tests/unit/test_gen_office200.py
#                  ::test_the_pin_is_the_digest_of_a_freshly_generated_corpus
#                  ~5 s. F2's 200 office documents (D656), pinned through a MANIFEST as the
#                  reference corpora are; `uv run python fixtures/gen/gen_office200.py --print-sha256`.
#   all of them    ::test_the_pin_file_names_every_generated_output_in_sha256sum_format asserts
#                  that this file names exactly these outputs and nothing else.
#
# The first two lines are not independent. The content of page i is a pure function of i, so the
# eight-page file is byte-for-byte the first eight pages of the 5,000-page one; that property is
# itself a test (::test_the_content_of_a_page_does_not_depend_on_the_page_count), which is what
# makes the cheap pin a real signal about the expensive one.
#
# The third is not independent of them either, and that is W4.10's whole reason for making
# gen_5000p_pdf.write_pdf public: every page of every document in the incremental corpus is a
# page_content(i) from the same frozen space, so the two PDF pins cover the incremental corpus's
# CONTENT and this third line covers which pages each document holds and in what order.

